Additive, self-contained. Exposes the raw Brandt mass pairing (the diagonal
inner product InnerProductMatrixBig computes internally) as a public intrinsic,
so the Delta' computation can read the monodromy pairing in the same basis as
InternalHMFRawHeckeDefiniteSparse. Apply on top of hmf-sparse-hecke.patch.

Two changes to ModFrmHil/definite.m:

1. A forward declaration, next to the existing `forward HeckeOperatorDefiniteBig;`
   (InnerProductMatrixBig is a function defined ~600 lines below the new
   intrinsic, so it must be forward-declared):

     forward HeckeOperatorDefiniteBig;
    +forward InnerProductMatrixBig;

2. A new intrinsic, immediately after InternalHMFRawHeckeDefiniteSparse
   (i.e. right before `intrinsic HeckeMatrixRaw`):

+intrinsic InternalHMFRawInnerProductDefinite(M::ModFrmHil) -> SeqEnum
+{The diagonal Brandt mass pairing on the raw space containing M (the natural
+ Hecke-invariant inner product), returned as the sequence of diagonal masses in
+ the same basis as InternalHMFRawHeckeDefiniteSparse.  Parallel weight 2 only.
+ This is the monodromy pairing on the character lattice of the Cerednik-Drinfeld
+ toric reduction (dembele/certificates/gate5-delta-prime-plan.md).}
+
+  require not assigned M`Ambient :
+         "This space is computed as a subspace of another space: use M`Ambient";
+  require Seqset(Weight(M)) eq {2} :
+         "Only implemented for parallel weight 2";
+
+  IP := InnerProductMatrixBig(M);
+  assert IsDiagonal(IP);
+  return [ Integers()! IP[i,i] : i in [1..Nrows(IP)] ];
+end intrinsic;
